@page "/components/input-group"

<PageTitle>Input Group — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Input Group</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    An icon, a button or a unit inside the field's own frame. The frame carries the focus ring
    rather than the input, because <code>:focus-within</code> is what makes a composite control
    look focused rather than look like two things next to each other.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="InputGroupExample.razor"><InputGroupExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Align</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Four places, named inline and block rather than left and right — which is what makes them
    follow the writing direction, and why the block ones grow a second row instead of squeezing
    the field.
</p>
<Example Source="InputGroupAlign.razor"><InputGroupAlign /></Example>

